msgid "OpenTelemetry Tracing"
msgstr "Rastreo OpenTelemetry"

msgid "If the xref:opentelemetry.adoc[OpenTelemetry extension] is present, the active trace context is automatically propagated from the signal emission to the receiver invocations."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Because receivers are executed asynchronously on a separate context, the trace context captured on the emitting thread would otherwise be lost.\n"
"To bridge this gap, when the signal is emitted the active context is captured into the signal metadata under the `quarkus.tracing` key -- as a map of https://www.w3.org/TR/trace-context/[W3C Trace Context] headers (e.g. `traceparent`) -- and restored when a receiver is invoked.\n"
"A new span is created for each receiver invocation.\n"
"When the signal is emitted within an active trace, the span is a child of the emitter's span, so a `publish` emission that reaches multiple receivers results in one child span per receiver.\n"
"Otherwise the span is started as a new root span (i.e. a new trace).\n"
"Each span is named `receive <signal type>` (where `<signal type>` is the raw signal type name) and carries the following attributes:"
msgstr ""

msgid "`signals.signal.type` -- the signal type, including generic type arguments if any (unlike the span name, which uses the raw type name),"
msgstr ""

msgid "`signals.emission.type` -- the emission type (`PUBLISH`, `SEND` or `REQUEST`),"
msgstr ""

msgid "`signals.response.type` -- the expected response type; only present for request-reply emissions,"
msgstr ""

msgid "`signals.qualifiers` -- the emission qualifiers, excluding the built-in `@Default` and `@Any`; only present if there is at least one such qualifier,"
msgstr ""

msgid "`signals.receiver` -- a human-readable name of the receiver; only present if available,"
msgstr ""

msgid "`signals.receiver.wait_ms` -- the time in milliseconds elapsed between the emission and the start of the receiver invocation."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the receiver fails, the span status is set to error and the exception is recorded together with the `error.type` attribute."
msgstr ""

